  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "After using the tool to export image binaries from fedora I am unable to look at those files anymore – a jpeg file will no longer open correctly and the SHA1 is different. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I suspect the wrong File object is used in exporting the object and it's not being treated like a binary file: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export/blob/0111580f9b4fb1714abe01d01accf674c92bba35/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/importexport/common/TransferProcess.java#L82"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export/blob/0111580f9b4fb1714abe01d01accf674c92bba35/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/importexport/common/TransferProcess.java#L82",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is on a mac OSx and to reproduce this issue create a binary file and export it.  I've seen this with a jpeg, but haven't tried other binary file formats. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
