  "description": "<p>After using the tool to export image binaries from fedora I am unable to look at those files anymore &#8211; a jpeg file will no longer open correctly and the SHA1 is different. </p>\n\n<p>I suspect the wrong File object is used in exporting the object and it's not being treated like a binary file: <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export/blob/0111580f9b4fb1714abe01d01accf674c92bba35/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/importexport/common/TransferProcess.java#L82\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export/blob/0111580f9b4fb1714abe01d01accf674c92bba35/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/importexport/common/TransferProcess.java#L82</a></p>\n\n<p>This is on a mac OSx and to reproduce this issue create a binary file and export it.  I've seen this with a jpeg, but haven't tried other binary file formats. </p>",
